WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.850
In nineteen ninety-eight, capsules made in a drug factory from the same powder by the same method suddenly became useless.

2
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:15.940
The molecule was the same, the formula was the same, the purity was the same — the only thing that had changed was the way the atoms were arranged.

3
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:21.030
And the old arrangement could never again be obtained in the laboratory, by any means.

4
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:35.760
Think of the pale, greyish bloom that creeps across a bar of chocolate left too long in the refrigerator.

5
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.610
The chocolate has not spoiled.

6
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.980
Nothing has contaminated it.

7
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.630
Its composition today is exactly what it was yesterday.

8
00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:50.200
The only thing that has changed is how the molecules of cocoa butter are arranged relative to one another.

9
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:57.210
The arrangement shifted, and with it the texture changed, the gloss disappeared, the melting point in the mouth moved.

10
00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:00.380
The same substance, two separate solids.

11
00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:04.990
Chemistry's quiet sleight of hand has a name: polymorphism.

12
00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:10.080
Its most familiar example is a pair everyone knows: graphite and diamond.

13
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.770
Both are pure carbon.

14
00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:19.940
One is soft enough to leave a black streak on paper from the tip of a pencil; the other is the hardest natural material known.

15
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:25.190
The chasm between them comes not from the identity of the atoms but from their architecture.

16
00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:30.440
In graphite, carbon atoms stack in layers that slide easily past one another.

17
00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:36.490
In diamond, every atom is bound tightly to four neighbours, building a three dimensional cage.

18
00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:41.260
How you pack molecules into a box determines what that box is.

19
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:45.870
In a crystal, molecules do not pile up at random.

20
00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:53.520
They settle into an order, a repeating pattern, and along that pattern hydrogen bonds form and lock the molecules to each other.

21
00:01:53.520 --> 00:02:00.530
It is entirely possible for the same molecule to settle into more than one such order, and each of those orders is called a form.

22
00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.020
The difference between forms is no academic nicety.

23
00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:10.870
The melting point changes, the density changes, the behaviour under pressure changes, even the colour can change.

24
00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:16.760
And when a medicine is involved, the most consequential of all: the solubility changes.

25
00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:21.690
Solubility, for a drug, is a matter of life and death.

26
00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:29.980
The tablet or capsule you swallow is useful only to the extent that it can dissolve its active ingredient in the fluid of your digestive system.

27
00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:40.510
A molecule that does not dissolve is not absorbed; a molecule that is not absorbed never reaches the bloodstream; and a molecule that never reaches the bloodstream does nothing in the patient's body,

28
00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:44.800
however brilliant a discovery it was in the laboratory.

29
00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:52.130
The difference in solubility between two crystal forms can decide whether the same dose is an effective therapy or an expensive nothing.

30
00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:56.900
Now to the molecule where that rule was tested in its most dramatic form.

31
00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:05.030
Ritonavir is a drug developed against HIV, blocking an enzyme called protease that the virus uses to process its own proteins.

32
00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:15.240
The middle of the 1990s was a period in which every month weighed heavily in HIV treatment; protease inhibitors were the missing piece of the combination therapies that, for the first time,

33
00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:19.690
could genuinely push back a disease nobody had been able to slow.

34
00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:28.460
Ritonavir was approved in the United States in March 1996 and brought to market under the name Norvir by Abbott Laboratories, or Abbott for short.

35
00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:36.910
It came in two forms: a 100 milligram capsule, and an oral solution carrying 80 milligrams of active ingredient per millilitre.

36
00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:41.360
But this molecule had a flaw: it barely dissolved in water.

37
00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:47.570
Filling a capsule with the powder and handing it to a patient would mean leaving most of the molecule undissolved in the gut.

38
00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:56.340
To get around this, the formulation team chose an elegant but bold route: they put ritonavir into the capsule not as a solid but already dissolved.

39
00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:02.390
They dissolved the molecule up front in a semi solid mixture containing ethanol and oleic acid.

40
00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:07.480
What reached the patient's stomach was now a liquid that did not have to wait to dissolve.

41
00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.810
That solution carried a subtle price.

42
00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:20.540
There is a ceiling on how much of a molecule you can dissolve in a given liquid, and in this formulation ritonavir sat just beneath that ceiling, close to the saturation limit.

43
00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:24.350
A solution near saturation walks a chemical tightrope.

44
00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:35.520
If a crystal form of lower solubility appears within it, that same solution becomes supersaturated with respect to the new form; the liquid, in other words, is now carrying more than it can hold.

45
00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:42.050
And such a liquid has only one thing to do: throw the excess out as a solid, and crystallise.

46
00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:47.780
Through the development years, Abbott's chemists knew only one crystal form of ritonavir.

47
00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:57.030
In this structure, later named Form I, the molecule folded on itself in a particular way and built a particular network of hydrogen bonds with its neighbours.

48
00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:05.160
The ritonavir molecule is long, flexible, bendable; molecules like this can settle into different crystals by folding differently.

49
00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:15.370
This is called conformational polymorphism: what changes is not merely the placement of molecules relative to one another, but the posture of the molecule itself.

50
00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:21.900
The critical point for ritonavir was that the carbamate group in its structure could point in two different directions.

51
00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:33.550
When that group turns the other way, the molecule folds differently, builds a different hydrogen bonding scheme, and the result is a more tightly interlocked crystal, one that demands more energy to come apart.

52
00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:38.480
Ritonavir, in short, had a second face that nobody had seen.

53
00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.490
A more stable, less soluble face.

54
00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:47.700
And the entire architecture of the formulation rested on the assumption that no such face existed.

55
00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:55.670
In mid 1998, two years after launch, a routine test in the quality control laboratory returned an unexpected result.

56
00:05:55.670 --> 00:06:08.280
A dissolution test measures whether a drug dissolves in a specified fluid, within a specified time, to a specified degree; it is among the most ordinary, most monotonous checks in the pharmaceutical industry.

57
00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:13.530
In July 1998, some batches of Norvir capsules failed it.

58
00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:18.780
Inside the capsules was something that should not have been there: solid particles.

59
00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:22.110
The solution was spitting its ritonavir back out.

60
00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:29.600
Placed under a microscope and examined by X ray powder diffraction, those particles left a fingerprint in their diffraction pattern.

61
00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:33.090
The pattern did not belong to Form I.

62
00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:38.980
It was a second crystal form of ritonavir, never before seen, and it was named Form II.

63
00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:45.350
Its worst property emerged immediately: Form II dissolved to less than half the extent of Form I.

64
00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:50.920
The ethanol based formulation was wildly supersaturated with respect to this new form.

65
00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:58.410
The moment Form II appeared, the liquid inside the capsule was no longer a solution but a reservoir waiting to crystallise.

66
00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:01.100
The real disaster came next.

67
00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:08.750
Once it had appeared, the new form spread within weeks across both the active ingredient production areas and the formulation areas.

68
00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:14.000
The reason is one of chemistry's most unnerving mechanisms: nucleation.

69
00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:21.810
For a crystal to form, a tiny nucleus, a seed, must first be established, and that first step is usually the hardest.

70
00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:30.260
If a molecule has never settled into a new form, there is no seed for that form, and a solution may carry on with its old habit for years.

71
00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:34.390
But once the seed exists, everything changes.

72
00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:46.680
A single microscopic particle, invisible, drifting in the air, settling on a bench, on the blade of a mixer, on a filter, on a technician's coat, shows the template to every saturated solution it touches.

73
00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:55.610
Those invisible seeds, scattered through every corner of the plant, gave the same answer to every process trying to make Form I: we make Form II now.

74
00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:57.980
And the reverse proved impossible.

75
00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:07.710
The same reactor, the same solvent, the same temperature profile, the same personnel, the same written procedure, and the result again was Form II.

76
00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:14.240
The form that had been produced without incident for two years could no longer be produced at all with the recipe in hand.

77
00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:19.810
Abbott spent a few million dollars on the manufacturing side trying to rescue the capsule.

78
00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:26.340
Different crystallisation conditions, different processing steps, cleaning strategies were tried.

79
00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:28.230
None of them held.

80
00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:35.880
In the end the company abandoned the attempt and, towards the close of 1998, the capsule was withdrawn from the market.

81
00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:41.290
The only option left was the oral solution, and that solution tasted terrible.

82
00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:52.460
At a meeting with patient representatives in October 1998, the company said it could supply enough liquid for the roughly 70,000 people using ritonavir worldwide; at the same meeting,

83
00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:58.510
the idea of chasing the liquid with something like chocolate or nut butter to mask the taste was discussed.

84
00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:02.160
And here the matter goes beyond supply logistics.

85
00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:11.250
A protease inhibitor regimen suppresses the virus only when it is sustained without missed days and without missed doses; otherwise resistance develops.

86
00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:18.100
A formulation that is hard to swallow is therefore not merely a comfort problem but a threat to the success of the treatment.

87
00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:28.470
On top of that, both the liquid and the capsule had to be kept refrigerated, a constraint that by itself made delivering the drug to every part of the world with equal confidence far harder.

88
00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:32.440
A new capsule returned to the market in 1999.

89
00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:45.850
This time the formulation was rebuilt to work in spite of Form II's existence: a soft elastic capsule containing polyoxyl 35 castor oil, butylated hydroxytoluene and gelatin alongside the oleic acid and ethanol.

90
00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:48.700
The engineering logic had been inverted.

91
00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:57.150
The aim was no longer to produce the desired crystal, but to accept the existence of the undesired one and design a carrier that could live with it.

92
00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:04.320
In 2000, Abbott's process chemists described what they had been through in the journal Organic Process Research and Development;

93
00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:12.450
among the things they described was that they had ultimately been forced to learn how to make Form II deliberately and reliably, rather than by accident.

94
00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:18.180
The cost of the whole crisis to Abbott is usually put at around 250 million dollars.

95
00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:22.470
One question remained, and it stood unanswered for years.

96
00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.520
Where did Form I go?

97
00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:30.250
Crystallography has a name for this phenomenon: the disappearing polymorph.

98
00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:36.620
A form becomes impossible to obtain in laboratories again once a more stable rival has walked onto the stage.

99
00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:47.950
Sometimes a team on the other side of the world applies the old recipe and finds the new form; sometimes a team pushes in the opposite direction, trying to bring back the lost one, and fails.

100
00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:50.960
There is nothing supernatural about this.

101
00:10:50.960 --> 00:11:01.970
It is the combination of two things: nature's constant tendency to flow towards the most stable structure, and the impossibility of eliminating that structure's seeds once they exist.

102
00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:13.780
The examples gathered over the years by Bernstein and colleagues showed that most disappearing polymorphs had not in fact vanished; the condition that would give birth to them had merely been forgotten, or never known.

103
00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:20.630
The condition that brought ritonavir's lost form back turned up somewhere no one would think to look for crystal growth: inside a mill.

104
00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:33.720
A study led by Aurora Cruz-Cabeza, with the participation of researchers at the University of Manchester, Durham University and in Cambridge, was published in 2024 in the Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences.

105
00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:43.770
The instrument the team used was a laboratory scale ball mill: a steel vessel, steel balls inside it, and a motor that flings the vessel back and forth 30 times a second.

106
00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:47.740
The powder is broken and reshaped over and over between the balls.

107
00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:57.630
Add a very small amount of liquid, a wetness on the order of a quarter of a microlitre per milligram, and a thin film forms that allows molecules to rearrange on the surfaces.

108
00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:01.440
The results ran in two directions, and both were striking.

109
00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:07.810
Milled with a drop of isopropyl alcohol, Form I converted to Form II within just a few minutes.

110
00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:14.820
The form that sealed off a factory in 1998 is, today, something you could find in a laboratory before lunch.

111
00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:25.510
The second direction was the more surprising one: with a drop of water, at room temperature, after about 150 minutes of milling, Form II converted completely back to Form I.

112
00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:29.000
The vanished crystal had not vanished.

113
00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:36.010
The reason is not an exception to thermodynamics but the fact that thermodynamics is sensitive to scale.

114
00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:45.580
When we calculate a crystal's stability we usually look at the energy of its interior, because in a large crystal the molecules sitting on the surface are a negligible fraction of the total.

115
00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:48.910
In the mill that balance breaks down.

116
00:12:48.910 --> 00:13:00.240
Once crystals are broken down to the order of 40 nanometres, a substantial share of the molecules begins to live on the surface, and surface energy becomes the decisive term in the arithmetic.

117
00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:09.490
The shape of the crystal joins in too; needle like elongated structures carry a great deal of surface relative to their volume, and so amplify the effect.

118
00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:16.820
Add to this the molecule's ability to change its own fold, and the stability ranking between the two forms can be reversed.

119
00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:24.950
Form II, the more stable one under normal conditions, is no longer the winning side at the nanometre scale with the right degree of wetness.

120
00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:34.520
The mill opens a new dial for the polymorph hunter: by changing the liquid, the duration and the ratio of wetness, you can deliberately tilt the stability ranking.

121
00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:37.850
Something similar matured on the computational side.

122
00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:47.580
A study published in 2025 in the journal Communications Chemistry by researchers at Merck set out to predict ritonavir's crystal structures from scratch on a computer.

123
00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:55.390
The method, called crystal structure prediction, generates every possible packing arrangement of the molecule and ranks them by energy.

124
00:13:55.390 --> 00:14:07.040
The result was unambiguous: around room temperature, the structure predicted to be most stable was the one corresponding to Form II, sitting about 1.62 kilojoules per mole below Form I.

125
00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:12.770
That is consistent with the measured difference, which falls in the range of 2 to 3 kilojoules.

126
00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:23.940
The authors' judgement is clear: had today's computational tools been available at the time, the existence of Form II and the formulation's intolerance of a drop in solubility could have been foreseen.

127
00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:35.110
The same study also solved, using 3 dimensional electron diffraction, the structure of a fourth form of ritonavir: needle shaped, carrying a disordered isopropyl group inside it,

128
00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:38.760
and markedly less stable than the other two forms.

129
00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:43.370
Ritonavir's own story, meanwhile, arrived somewhere else.

130
00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:51.340
The tablet formulation approved in 2010 follows a path that solves the polymorph problem at the root: hot melt extrusion.

131
00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:59.470
The active ingredient is melted and mixed together with a polymer, and what emerges is an amorphous solid dispersion that has never crystallised at all.

132
00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:08.880
Where there is no crystal there is no polymorph; what remains is to prevent the amorphous structure from crystallising over time, which is precisely the polymer's job.

133
00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:14.130
The tablet can be stored at room temperature and Form II does not appear inside it.

134
00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:18.420
The cold chain constraint thereby passed into history.

135
00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:31.190
The molecule itself found a second career: ritonavir today is mostly used not to suppress HIV directly but as a booster, slowing an enzyme in the liver so that the drug taken alongside it stays in the blood longer.

136
00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:38.360
The second component of the nirmatrelvir and ritonavir combination used in Covid 19 treatment is the same molecule.

137
00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:45.210
What stopped a factory in 1998 was not a virus, not sabotage, not a calculation error.

138
00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:50.780
It was a second way of folding, belonging to the same molecule, that nobody had seen.

139
00:15:50.780 --> 00:16:01.310
Finding that form takes half a day in a laboratory today; and the old crystal that its seeds took from us comes back inside a steel vessel, milled with the right liquid for the right length of time.

140
00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:05.280
Nöron Science'de bugünkü bölümün sonuna geldik.

141
00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:08.290
Yeni bir hikâyede yeniden buluşmak üzere.
